From db1277aefb790168f0c7b5940f15c15f3a3f9bf0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Quintin Smits <qd.smits@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 28 Nov 2026 05:29:25 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 4/7] feat(app): rename a tool with its operations in one undo
 step

RenameTool changes the tool's name and the tool reference of each
operation that uses it, as one undo step. It refuses an empty name, a
clash, an unknown name, a non-tool, the same name, a setup name, a name
that an operation still names and a machine-reserved name, by name. An
up-to-date operation stays up to date.

The MCP tool rename_tool calls the same command. The tool library
editor's Name row is a text field; Apply lands the typed name, and the
views that show the tool follow it (also on undo and redo).

Fixes #4370

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
